<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mario Vargas Llosa</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1936–2025</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mario Vargas Llosa was a Peruvian novelist and essayist, a leading figure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> American literary boom, who won the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Literature in 2010. His novels include The Time of the Hero (1963), Conversation in the Cathedral (1969) and The Feast of the Goat (2000). Turning from the left to liberalism, he ran for the presidency of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> in 1990 and lost to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberto-fujimori">Alberto Fujimori</a>. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lima">Lima</a> in 2025.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mario-vargas-llosa.jpg" alt="Mario Vargas Llosa" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gotfryd · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mario_Vargas_Llosa_LCCN2020733847_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
